From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] standby: de-glitch same-second wakes, record wake source (debug)

Every board run woke ~0.13 s after entering deep standby, always inside
the clk_suspend/clk_resume window (the "wakeup: %d" print lands in the
UART divider change and is lost in garble), even with ehci1/ohci1
unbound and the R-PIO registration refused. Whatever the impostor is
(clock-switch noise, PMU NMI line state), a wake that lands in the same
RTC second the entry sequence ran cannot be a real request: record it in
the always-on RTC_GPR0 (0xED000000|src, printed at the next
standby_init) and keep waiting. Real sources (the +20 s RTC alarm in our
tests, the power key) land in a later second and are accepted, printed
readably and recorded as 0xEE000000|src.
--- a/ar100s/service/standby/standby-sun60iw2p1/plat_standby.c
+++ b/ar100s/service/standby/standby-sun60iw2p1/plat_standby.c
@@ -322,9 +322,12 @@
 
 static void wait_wakeup(void)
 {
+	u32 sec_entry;
+
 	save_state_flag(REC_ESTANDBY | REC_WAIT_WAKEUP | 0x01);
 	wakeup_timer_start();
 	//wakeup_source = NO_WAKESOURCE;
+	sec_entry = readl(RTC_HMS) & RTC_HMS_S_MASK;
 	while (1) {
 		/*
 		 * maybe add user defined task process here
@@ -332,7 +335,25 @@
 
 
 		if (wakeup_source != NO_WAKESOURCE) {
-			LOG("wakeup: %d\n", wakeup_source);
+			/*
+			 * De-glitch (debug): every board run so far woke ~0.13 s
+			 * after entry, inside the clk_suspend/clk_resume window
+			 * where the UART divider is mid-change -- a wake landing
+			 * in the same RTC second the entry sequence ran is clock-
+			 * switch noise or the PMU NMI line state, not a wake
+			 * request (the RTC alarm in our tests fires 20 s later).
+			 * Record the impostor in the always-on RTC_GPR0 and keep
+			 * waiting. A real wake (RTC alarm, power key) always lands
+			 * in a later second and is accepted.
+			 */
+			if ((readl(RTC_HMS) & RTC_HMS_S_MASK) == sec_entry) {
+				writel(0xED000000u | wakeup_source, RTC_GPR0);
+				LOG("ignore early wake %d\n", wakeup_source);
+				wakeup_source = NO_WAKESOURCE;
+				continue;
+			}
+			writel(0xEE000000u | wakeup_source, RTC_GPR0);
+			LOG("wake src: %d\n", wakeup_source);
 			break;
 		}
 		/* e902 low power mode */
--- a/ar100s/service/standby/standby.c
+++ b/ar100s/service/standby/standby.c
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@
 
 	wakeup_timer_init();
 
+	/* debug: wake-source records of the previous standby attempt
+	 * (0xED/0xEE000000|src in RTC_GPR0, see plat_standby.c); survives a
+	 * warm reboot, cleared by a full power cut. */
+	LOG("last wake record: %x\n", readl(RTC_GPR0));
+
 	return OK;
 }
 
